//
// Risograph print / リソグラフ
// Pack: artstyle (Art styles for image generation) · element 13 · Category: Graphic styles
// What happens: The same line drawing becomes a print in two inks, yellow and teal; the two layers overlap slightly out of register, with ink grain and paper texture visible.
// Motion spec:
//   - Medium: stencil printing with two or three inks (Risograph)
//   - Look: misregistration between layers, ink grain and paper texture stand out; the sample uses yellow and teal
//   - Note: two colors blended smoothly look like a duotone (#116); keep the offset and grain
//   - Sample: the same base sketch (a line drawing of a house, a tree and the sun on a hill) was given to an image model as a reference and redrawn in this style. A diagonal wipe turns the sketch into the style from 0.5 s to 1.35 s, the picture slowly zooms to 1.045x until 4.0 s, and it fades back to the sketch from 4.0 s to 4.5 s (one pass = 4.7 s, cubic ease-in-out)
// When to use it: For the feel of zines, flyers and indie posters.
// Tags: risograph, riso, print, misregistration, grain, zine
// Size: 539x208 px · Cycle: 4.7 s
// Needs: kit artstyle -> https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/api/v1/kit/artstyle.js
// Live demo: https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#205
//
// cells[i](k, w, h, u): k = CanvasRenderingContext2D (already cleared and wrapped in save/restore by the caller), w,h = size, u = seconds in [0, cycle). The picture depends only on u.
// Element code starts here. CELLS, constants and helpers live in the kit.

// @element 13
// リソグラフ: 2〜3色のインクがずれて重なる
CELLS[12] = (k, w, h, u) => gafu(k, w, h, u, '13');
